WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.585
Need a due date, a follow up date, or last year's date?

2
00:00:04.585 --> 00:00:06.477
M functions do it for you.

3
00:00:06.477 --> 00:00:10.892
In this lesson, you will learn to add years, months and days to a

4
00:00:10.892 --> 00:00:15.308
date in a custom column, read the hints Power Query gives you, and fix

5
00:00:15.308 --> 00:00:17.200
the most common errors. Let's go!

6
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.045
On the Add Column tab, open Custom Column.

7
00:00:22.045 --> 00:00:27.200
I name the new column twenty twenty three, and start typing Date dot Add.

8
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.638
IntelliSense lists every function that matches:

9
00:00:36.638 --> 00:00:40.688
Date dot AddDays, AddMonths, AddQuarters, AddWeeks, and AddYears.

10
00:00:40.688 --> 00:00:43.220
Pick the one you need.

11
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.304
I choose Date dot AddYears.

12
00:01:00.304 --> 00:01:01.668
It needs two things:

13
00:01:01.668 --> 00:01:04.736
a date, and the number of years to add.

14
00:01:04.736 --> 00:01:06.440
I insert the today column.

15
00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.100
Notice the message: Token Eof expected.

16
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.600
The formula is not finished yet.

17
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.100
We still need the second argument.

18
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.635
When I click OK too early, the new column fills with errors.

19
00:01:25.635 --> 00:01:29.080
Each error tells us something is missing in the formula.

20
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.404
Let's try Date dot AddMonths.

21
00:01:40.404 --> 00:01:42.209
I name the column April.

22
00:01:42.209 --> 00:01:44.013
The hint shows the arguments:

23
00:01:44.013 --> 00:01:46.900
a date time, and the number of months.

24
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.522
I add the today column and the number one.

25
00:02:13.522 --> 00:02:16.120
Now each date moves forward by one month.

26
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.991
Back to AddYears, this time done right:

27
00:02:25.991 --> 00:02:29.407
the today column, a comma, and the number of years.

28
00:02:29.407 --> 00:02:32.140
Now the new column shows the correct dates.

29
00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.036
The rule is simple:

30
00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:53.625
read the hint, give every argument, and close every bracket.

31
00:02:53.625 --> 00:02:55.420
Practice with your own dates!

